Dear Capstone Program Team,

Please find below Team Hellites' Round 1 submission for the Orchard case.

Team details
- Team name: Hellites
- Campus: IIM Lucknow
- Case solved: Orchard (Alderbrook Beverage Company)
- Kumar Ashwini (PGP41426), Team Member - Hellites, IIM Lucknow =E2=80=93 MBA=
, Class of 2027
- Pankaj Goswami (PGP41434), Team Member - Hellites, IIM Lucknow =E2=80=93 MB=
A, Class of 2027

Solution
- Interactive dashboard (no login or payment required): https://ashu481g.gith=
ub.io/Delloite-US/
  The core solution can be explored in under 10 minutes; a reviewer guide is =
at the top of the page.
- PDF summary of our analysis and recommendation: IIML_Hellites_Orchard.pdf (=
attached)

Recommendation in brief
Acquire Brightwater Botanicals through a structured, pay-for-proof deal ($300=
M at close, $50M founder and PE rollover equity, and up to $100M in earn-outs=
 tied to conventional-channel velocity and revenue milestones). This closes t=
he FY29 revenue and functional-revenue gaps while keeping net debt / EBITDA a=
t 2.48x, within the board's 2.5x limit.

How we used AI and validated its outputs
We used Claude (Anthropic) to structure the issue tree, check the case arithm=
etic, build and stress-test the financial model, challenge our option scoring=
, and scaffold the dashboard code. Every figure was checked against the case =
exhibits, and the Excel model and the dashboard produce identical results. As=
sumptions are labelled as such and were reviewed and set by the team. The cho=
ice of option, the deal structure, the scoring weights and the final recommen=
dation are our team's own judgment.

Attachments
1. IIML_Hellites_Orchard.pdf (solution summary)
2. Kumar_Ashwini_PGP41426_CV.pdf
3. Pankaj_Goswami_PGP41434_CV.pdf

Thank you for the opportunity. We look forward to your feedback.

Regards,
Kumar Ashwini and Pankaj Goswami
Team Hellites, IIM Lucknow

